#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:15
msgid "Interpolation of Values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:17
msgid ""
"In addition to its core functionality, PlatformIO introduces support for "
"interpolation, allowing values to incorporate format strings that reference "
"other values from different sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:21
msgid "The interpolation feature adheres to the following syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:23
msgid ""
"``${<variable>}``, where ``<variable>`` represents the name of a supported "
"built-in variable (refer to the table below for details)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:25
msgid ""
"``${<section>.<option>}``, with ``<section>`` denoting a value from the "
"``[<section>]`` group, and ``<option>`` representing the first item in the "
"pair ``<option> = value``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:32
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:33
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:34
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:36
msgid "``${<variable>}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:37
msgid ""
"Incorporate built-in variables using their designated names. The following "
"variables are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:40
msgid "``PROJECT_DIR`` - represents the current project directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:41
msgid "``PROJECT_HASH`` - corresponds to the hash of the project path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:42
msgid ""
"``UNIX_TIME`` - indicates the current  `Unix time <https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/Unix_time>`__, represented by 10 digits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:45
msgid ""
"``/tmp/pio-workspaces/${PROJECT_HASH}`` refers to the new directory ``/tmp/"
"pio-workspaces/project_name-8f66e9463d/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:47
msgid "``${sysenv.<name>}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:48
msgid "Embed operating system environment variable by a name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:49
msgid "``${sysenv.HOME}`` refers to the user home directory on Unix machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:51
msgid "``${platformio.<option>}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:52
msgid "Embed value from :ref:`projectconf_section_platformio`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:53
msgid ""
"``${platformio.packages_dir}`` refers to the path of :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_packages_dir`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:55
msgid "``${env.<option>}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:56
msgid "Embed default value from :ref:`projectconf_section_env`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:57
msgid "``${env.debug_build_flags}`` refers to the default debugging flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:59
msgid "``${<section>.<option>}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:60
msgid "Embed value from another section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:61
msgid ""
"``${extra.lib_deps}`` embeds library dependencies declared in the section "
"named ``extra``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:63
msgid "``${this.<option>}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:64
msgid "Embed value from the current section without declaring a section name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:65
msgid "``${this.board}`` refers to the \"board\" value of the current section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:67
msgid "``${this.__env__}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:68
msgid ""
"Embed environment name of the current section. The section must start with "
"``env:`` prefix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:69
msgid ""
"``${this.__env__}`` will embed \"foo\" value being declared in the \"env:"
"foo\" section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:71
msgid "Interpolation can span multiple levels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:72
msgid "Interpolation can be applied only for the option's value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:73
msgid "Multiple interpolations are allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:74
msgid ""
"The :ref:`projectconf_section_platformio` and :ref:`projectconf_section_env` "
"sections are reserved and could not be used as a custom section. Some good "
"section names might be ``extra`` or ``custom``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/interpolation.rst:79
msgid ""
"If you need to **share common configuration options** between build "
"environments, please take a look at **\"Global scope\"** in :ref:"
"`projectconf_section_env` or :ref:`projectconf_env_extends` option which "
"allows extending of other sections."
msgstr ""

